        "containers": [
          {
            "resources": {
              "limits": {
                "memory": "128Mi"
              },
              "requests": {
                "memory": "64Mi"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```

I will apply this patch now.

The patch failed again, this time reporting: `The Deployment "app" is invalid: spec.template.spec.containers[0].image: Required value`.

This suggests that when I try to patch a container, Kubernetes requires all required fields (like `image`, `name`, etc.) to be present in the patch object, even if I only want to change `resources`. This is typical behavior when patching complex nested objects in Kubernetes.

I must provide a complete specification for the container I am modifying, including its existing required fields, while only changing the memory limits and requests.

I will retrieve the current container definition again, extract all required fields, and then construct the patch to only modify the resources.

