The container definition is:
```yaml
      - image: nginx:1.31.5
        imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent
        name: app
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
          name: http
          protocol: TCP
        readinessProbe:
          failureThreshold: 1
          periodSeconds: 2
          successThreshold: 1
          tcpSocket:
            port: http
          timeoutSeconds: 1
        resources:
          limits:
            memory: 4Mi
        terminationMessagePath: /dev/termination-log
        terminationMessagePolicy: File
```

The patch should look like this (keeping everything, but overriding `resources`):
```json
{
  "spec": {
    "template": {
      "spec": {
        "containers": [
          {
            "image": "nginx:1.31.5",
            "imagePullPolicy": "IfNotPresent",
            "name": "app",
            "ports": [
              {
                "containerPort": 80,
                "name": "http",
                "protocol": "TCP"
              }
            ],
            "readinessProbe": {
              "failureThreshold": 1,
              "periodSeconds": 2,
              "successThreshold": 1,
              "tcpSocket": {
                "port": "http"
              },
              "timeoutSeconds": 1
            },
            "resources": {
              "limits": {
                "memory": "128Mi"
              },
              "requests": {
                "memory": "64Mi"
              }
            },
            "terminationMessagePath": "/dev/termination-log",
            "terminationMessagePolicy": "File"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
This is a large, complex patch, but it adheres to the required structure for a merge patch when modifying an element within an array. I will execute this.

Since the patch is complex, I will use `kubectl apply` with a modified manifest, as it is safer and handles required fields more gracefully than a complex merge patch. I will generate the minimal necessary patch to apply to the deployment.

I will create a temporary manifest file with the updated deployment specification and apply it.

